## Design Rules

- Decisions the design rests on are recorded in [decisions/](decisions/README.md).
{%- if stack == 'dotnet' %}
- Warnings are errors ([ADR-0100](decisions/project-template/0100-warnings-are-errors-in-every-project.md)), and disallowed APIs are banned at build time ([ADR-0102](decisions/project-template/0102-disallowed-apis-are-banned-at-build-time.md)).
{%- endif %}
{%- if library %}
- The public API is tracked and evolves compatibly ([ADR-0131](decisions/project-template/0131-public-api-is-tracked-and-evolves-compatibly.md)), and each package is validated against the last published package ([ADR-0147](decisions/project-template/0147-packages-are-validated-against-the-last-published-package.md)).
{%- endif %}

## Build and Release

CI runs the project's commands on every {{ pr }} (`{{ '.github/workflows/ci.yml' if git_host == 'github' else '.gitlab-ci.yml' }}`). {% if ghlib %}Releases are tagged and published as [ADR-0016](decisions/project-template/0016-releases-are-tagged-and-published-when-their-pull-request-merges.md) records.{% else %}Releases are tagged, and published, once `AGENTS.md`'s Landing section sets `release: tag` or `tag+release`, as [ADR-0016](decisions/project-template/0016-releases-are-tagged-and-published-when-their-pull-request-merges.md) records; it starts with `release: none`.{% endif %}
{%- if ghlib %} `publish.yml` tests and packs the tagged commit, pushes to nuget.org through trusted publishing once a maintainer approves the `nuget` environment, and calls `release-provenance.yml` and `raise-baseline.yml` ([ADR-0137](decisions/project-template/0137-the-release-workflow-starts-package-publishing.md), [ADR-0151](decisions/project-template/0151-release-follow-ups-are-jobs-publish-calls.md)).{% endif %}
